1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,290
Listen to a talk in a neuroscience class.

2
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:05,154
Man: Let's talk a little about language acquisition,

3
00:00:05,154 --> 00:00:09,290
which is the process by which humans learn to understand and use language.

4
00:00:09,290 --> 00:00:12,720
There are two main types of language acquisition

5
00:00:13,540 --> 00:00:17,070
first language acquisition and second language acquisition.

6
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:20,340
First language acquisition occurs naturally

7
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:23,028
and with relative ease during early childhood,

8
00:00:23,028 --> 00:00:27,000
through interaction with family and the surrounding environment.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,650
Children are able to pick up their native language quickly due to their innate linguistic capabilities,

10
00:00:32,650 --> 00:00:37,240
a concept supported by the linguist Noam Chomsky's theory of Universal Grammar.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:42,802
Universal Grammar suggests that the ability to acquire language is innate to humans

12
00:00:42,802 --> 00:00:47,080
and that all human languages share a common underlying structure.

13
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:50,130
Second language acquisition, on the other hand,

14
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:52,940
often requires more conscious effort

15
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:56,230
and formal education and typically happens later in life.

16
00:00:56,230 --> 00:01:01,944
Several factors influence the ease and success of second language acquisition,

17
00:01:01,944 --> 00:01:06,100
including exposure to the language, age, and motivation.

18
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:09,940
Motivation, in particular, plays a crucial role

19
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,127
highly motivated individuals are more likely to engage actively

20
00:01:13,127 --> 00:01:17,080
with the language and persist in their learning efforts.

21
00:01:17,080 --> 00:01:21,136
Age is also significant; according to the critical period hypothesis,

22
00:01:21,136 --> 00:01:24,940
there is an optimal window in early childhood during

23
00:01:24,940 --> 00:01:27,220
which language acquisition occurs most easily.

24
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:32,030
After this period, acquiring a new language can be more challenging.

25
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:34,113
Understanding these processes helps educators

26
00:01:34,113 --> 00:01:38,280
and linguists develop effective teaching methods and language learning tools.
